WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.730
Look at this sentence.

2
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.770
"The cat licked its paw.

3
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.030
" The paw belongs to the cat.

4
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.750
And an apostrophe can show
that something belongs,

5
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.830
like "the dog's lead".

6
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.050
So shouldn't there be an
apostrophe before the s?

7
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.830
Or is that a mistake?

8
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.310
One tiny mark, and the
whole meaning can shift.

9
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.520
In this mission, you'll learn
the two jobs of the apostrophe.

10
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.410
You'll find out why a comma
alone can't join two sentences.

11
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.930
You'll meet the colon
and the semicolon,

12
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.430
and you'll punctuate speech.

13
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.540
Your mission: decide whether this
sentence needs an apostrophe.
